cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "JASPER: An extensible benchmarking framework for JVM data serializers"
type: software

message: "If you use Jasper in your research, please cite this software."

abstract: >
  Jasper is an extensible benchmarking framework for systematically evaluating
  data serializers in modern JVM-based cloud-native environments. It combines
  correctness and robustness testing, serializer microbenchmarks, POSIX-level
  memory-operation baselines, and cloud-native macrobenchmarks based on web API
  and NLP workloads. The framework supports widely used JVM serializers,
  including Java serialization, dsljson, Jackson, GraalDoss, Gson, fastjson2,
  and Kryo. Its modular architecture, extensible workload generator,
  command-line client, and web dashboard enable reproducible local and remote
  experiments and facilitate comparisons of serialization technologies under
  different experimental conditions.

keywords:
  - benchmarking
  - data serialization
  - JVM
  - cloud-native
  - Java
  - serialization performance
  - memory behavior
  - microbenchmarks
  - macrobenchmarks
  - reproducible research

